  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fourth Phase Interventions in the Aquaculture valu</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project has strengthened the capacity of small producers in Niassa and Inhambane which are currently better skilled in the aquaculture value chain. - The aim of the project is to improve the value-chain of food systems, specifically in aquaculture, by strengthening the capacity of small-scale producers to increase their production volumes and sales, contributing to improved livelihoods and nutritional security. The project will be implemented in Inhambane and Niassa Provinces and will reach mostly youth and women. _x000D_
_x000D_
This year&#x2019;s project will level up the work that is being done by Chicoa Fish farm for about three years in Inhambane and Niassa Provinces, through capacity strengthening of fish producers in the fish farming value chain.</narrative>
  </description>
